      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through the following mechanism:\n\n**A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it directly into the environment of the spawned child process (the Ingest agent) immediately before that process starts.** The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential.\n\nThis design means:\n- A compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables\n- The key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API\n- The same scoping model applies to the Query agent process\u2014it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from the Hub\n\nThis is a credential isolation strategy that limits exposure to only the child processes that actually need the key.",
      "input_tokens": 2622,
      "output_tokens": 202
    }
